{"mathdb_id": 380052, "uuid": "e3a146e6-bb16-42c3-be5a-28337123e686", "canonical_url": "https://mathdb.com/p/380052/conjecture-on-the-limiting-distribution-of-random-cayley-gra", "title": "Conjecture on the limiting distribution of random Cayley graph diameters", "statement": "Let $q$ be prime, let $g_1,\ldots,g_k$ be independent uniformly random generators of the cyclic group ${\mathbb Z}_q$, and let $Diam(q,k)$ denote the diameter of the resulting directed Cayley graph. The same notation may be used for the corresponding undirected Cayley graph with generating set $\{g_1,-g_1,\ldots,g_k,-g_k\}$. **Diameter distribution conjecture.** The normalized diameter

$$
\frac{Diam(q,k)}{\sqrt[k]{q}}
$$

converges in distribution to some distribution $D(k)$ on ${\mathbb R}$ whose support is non-compact. The preceding upper and lower bounds show that the normalization by $\sqrt[k]{q}$ is of the correct order and that the limiting behavior is non-degenerate in the stated sense; the existence and non-compactness of the limiting distribution remain open in the source.", "statement_completeness": "full", "post_type": "conjecture", "status": "open", "tags": ["additive-combinatorics", "probability", "random-cayley-graphs"], "importance": "corpus", "source_name": "Gideon Amir and Ori Gurel-Gurevich, “The diameter of a random Cayley graph of Z_q”, arXiv:math/0609620 (2009).", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0609620", "first_stated_year": 2006, "first_stated_year_source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0609620", "documented_by_year": null, "documented_by_source_url": null, "references": "Source: https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0609620

